patrick","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"}],"name":"Export Finance and Insurance Corporation Amendment (Equity Investments and Other Measures) Bill 2021 - in Committee - Keep bill as is","noes":7,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2021-10-18.185.1) to keep [the bill](https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fbillhome%2Fr6749%22) as it is. In parliamentary jargon, they voted \"*that the bill stand as printed*\". ### What does this bill do? According to the [bills digest](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/bd/bd2122a/22bd016): > *The purpose of the [Export Finance and Insurance Corporation Amendment (Equity Investments and Other Measures) Bill 2021](https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fbillhome%2Fr6749%22) (the Bill) is to give legislative effect to the Government’s decision to broaden the range of transactions that [Export Finance Australia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Export_Finance_Australia) (EFA) can finance.* > > *Specifically, the Bill will amend the Export Finance and Insurance Corporation Act 1991 (the EFIC Act) to:* > > * *permit EFA to make equity investments and* > * *permit EFA Australia to offer standalone guarantees for overseas infrastructure transactions.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-7444","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2021-10-18/4"}
